refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.parameters;
data
The serialized session data, in the format of session.serialize_handler, as returned by session_encode. The data is not written to the session storage until the session is written, for example by session_write_close.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
&return.success;
If no session is active, an E_WARNING is emitted and &false; is returned. If the data cannot be decoded, an E_WARNING is emitted, &false; is returned and the session is destroyed: its data is deleted from the storage, $_SESSION becomes an empty array, session_status returns PHP_SESSION_NONE and session_id returns an empty string.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    7.0.0

     An E_WARNING is now emitted when no session is active.
     Previously, &false; was returned silently.
